        "output": "A single dark-themed HTML file with labeled components, arrows for HTTPS and cache traffic, and three summary cards."
      },
      {
        "input": "An AWS deployment with CloudFront, S3, load balancer, API servers, and database.",
        "output": "A cloud architecture diagram with an AWS region boundary, service groups, security annotations, and a legend outside the boundary."
      },
      {
        "input": "A security review diagram for public entry points, private services, and sensitive data stores.",
        "output": "A static diagram that separates identity, public access, private services, and data stores with dashed trust boundaries."
      }
    ],
    "best_practices": [
      "List required components, owners, ports, and data flows before generating the diagram.",
      "Keep legends outside boundaries and expand the SVG viewBox when space is needed.",
      "Remove the external font link when offline use or privacy is required."
    ],
    "anti_patterns": [
      "Do not place legends or message buses over component boundaries.",
      "Do not include secrets, real tokens, or private endpoint details in labels.",
      "Do not assume the diagram verifies the deployed architecture."
